-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ו/3 (27.1.2016): ניכוי שכר לעובדי הוראה בשל השבתת מערכת החינוך בשנת הלימודים התשע"ו
-- The deduction of pay from teaching staff who took part in the strike the
-- Teachers' Organization announced for 27.1.2016 until 10:00: no pay for
-- strike time, deduction by the hours absent at the hourly value (stay and
-- individual hours included), the attendance reports it rests on, the
-- presumption against an employee with no report, and the ministry's own
-- deduction from its payments to the owners.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ו/3 — ניכוי שכר בשל השבתה`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13 The letterhead, the date (27.1.2016), the reference number, the addressee, the greeting and the subject line; no rule.

DECLARE `strike action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct the strike hours from the salary` HAS `amount deducted` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct from the owner's current payments` HAS `amount withheld` IS A NUMBER

@desc A teaching employee on the strike day (27.1.2016), as far as the deduction asks about it.
DECLARE `strike-day case` HAS
    `reported attendance at the time of the strike`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `produced an approval for the absence`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc an approval of the absence under the procedures
    `produced proof of presence at work`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `took part in the strike by the attendance reports`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours absent during the strike`                        IS A NUMBER  @desc hours absent from work during the strike (to 10:00), stay hours and individual hours due then included
    `hourly value`                                          IS A NUMBER  @desc the employee's hourly value; an input

DECLARE `kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `a strike day`
    `a partial-strike day`
    `a day with no strike`

-- ¶14: by Government decisions 647 (22.4.80) and 646 (26.5.81) no pay is
-- paid for strike days and only partial pay for partial-strike days; in the
-- budgeted bodies section 29 of the Budget Foundations Law requires it.
-- The paragraph does not say how the partial pay is measured; for this
-- circular's strike ¶18 measures it by the hours absent.
@ref akn:hc_1/p14
GIVEN `the day` IS A `kind of day`
      `the day's full pay` IS A NUMBER
      `the partial pay` IS A NUMBER @desc the pay for the part of the day not struck; ¶14 does not measure it (an input)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the pay payable for the day` `the day` `the day's full pay` `the partial pay` IS
    CONSIDER `the day`
    WHEN `a strike day`         THEN 0
    WHEN `a partial-strike day` THEN min `the partial pay` `the day's full pay`
    WHEN `a day with no strike` THEN `the day's full pay`

-- ¶15–¶16: where teaching staff took part in the strike announced for today
-- until 10:00, the owner must deduct from their pay by the hours they were
-- absent; the deduction is made by the attendance reports at their places
-- of work. The circular sets no deadline for the deduction.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN c IS A `strike-day case`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `strike action`
DECIDE `deducting the strike hours` c IS
    IF `took part in the strike` c
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `deduct the strike hours from the salary` `amount`
               PROVIDED `amount` EQUALS `the strike deduction` c
         LEST BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "circular 2015-16/3: the owner must deduct from the pay of those who took part in the strike by the hours they were absent"
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN c IS A `strike-day case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `took part in the strike` c IF
    c's `took part in the strike by the attendance reports` OR `held to have taken part` c

-- ¶17: an employee who did not report attendance at the time of the strike,
-- and produced neither an approval of the absence under the procedures nor
-- proof of presence at work, is held to have taken part in the strike or
-- the organizational measures.
@ref akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN c IS A `strike-day case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `held to have taken part` c IF
        (NOT c's `reported attendance at the time of the strike`)
    AND (NOT c's `produced an approval for the absence`)
    AND (NOT c's `produced proof of presence at work`)

-- ¶18: the reduction is the time absent (in hours) times the hourly value;
-- stay hours and individual hours due during the strike are deducted too.
@ref akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN c IS A `strike-day case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the strike deduction` c IS
    IF `took part in the strike` c
    THEN c's `hours absent during the strike` TIMES c's `hourly value`
    ELSE 0

-- ¶19: the ministry deducts from its current payments to the owner by the
-- hours budgeted at the striking institutions and the times of the strike.
@ref akn:hc_1/p19
GIVEN `budgeted hours at the striking institutions during the strike` IS A NUMBER
      `the budgeted hourly cost` IS A NUMBER @desc the amount withheld per budgeted hour; the circular does not set it (an input)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the ministry's deduction from the owner` `budgeted hours at the striking institutions during the strike` `the budgeted hourly cost` IS
    `budgeted hours at the striking institutions during the strike` TIMES `the budgeted hourly cost`

-- akn:conclusions The signature (Sonia Peretz) and the list of copies; no rule.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- The hourly value of 100 is a placeholder.
`a teacher with no report, two hours due before 10:00` MEANS
    `strike-day case` WITH
        `reported attendance at the time of the strike`     IS FALSE
        `produced an approval for the absence`              IS FALSE
        `produced proof of presence at work`                IS FALSE
        `took part in the strike by the attendance reports` IS FALSE
        `hours absent during the strike`                    IS 2
        `hourly value`                                      IS 100

`a teacher with a sick-leave approval` MEANS
    `strike-day case` WITH
        `reported attendance at the time of the strike`     IS FALSE
        `produced an approval for the absence`              IS TRUE
        `produced proof of presence at work`                IS FALSE
        `took part in the strike by the attendance reports` IS FALSE
        `hours absent during the strike`                    IS 2
        `hourly value`                                      IS 100

#ASSERT `the strike deduction` `a teacher with no report, two hours due before 10:00` EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `the strike deduction` `a teacher with a sick-leave approval` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the pay payable for the day` `a strike day` 600 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the pay payable for the day` `a partial-strike day` 600 400 EQUALS 400

#TRACE `deducting the strike hours` `a teacher with no report, two hours due before 10:00` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `deduct the strike hours from the salary` 200 AT 1
